.TH EASYSTREAM 1 "2026-11-12" "easystream" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
easystream \- screen capture, input injection and an accessibility tree over est://
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B easystream
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B easystream
is the daemon half of a two-process design. It owns the screen, the pointer, the keyboard
and the platform's accessibility tree, and publishes them on two channels:
.TP
.B est:// (TCP, 48079)
One connection carrying the H.264 video stream, input events and clipboard. Input shares
the connection with the video so that a gesture is ordered against the frame it acts on.
.TP
.B HTTP (48078)
Discrete requests: the accessibility tree, one-shot screenshots, input primitives, and the
web UI at
.BR / .
.PP
A viewer, or
.BR easyworker ,
connects to it. This program does not decide what to do with the screen; it makes the
screen reachable.
.SH OPTIONS
The daemon is configured through the environment, because it is normally started by a
session unit rather than typed at a prompt.
.TP
.B EASYSTREAM_PORT
The est port. Default 48079.
.TP
.B EASYSTREAM_HTTP_PORT
The HTTP and WebSocket port. Default 48078.
.TP
.B EASYSTREAM_AUDIO_SOURCE
The PipeWire or PulseAudio source to record. Default
.BR vsink.monitor .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/easystream.service
The user unit. It is installed but not enabled:
.B systemctl --user enable --now easystream
.TP
.I /usr/share/easystream/
The web UI served at
.BR / .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start it in the current session and open the UI:
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl --user start easystream
xdg-open http://127.0.0.1:48078/
.RE
.fi
.PP
Ask what the daemon decided it can do:
.PP
.nf
.RS
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:48078/capabilities | jq
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.B libx264's ABI is part of the package.
.PP
This daemon links libx264, whose ABI number appears in both the SONAME and every exported
symbol
.RB ( libx264.so.164
exports
.BR x264_encoder_open_164 ).
A package built against one ABI does not run against another, and no dependency string can
express it. The package name carries the base it was built for; installing the one that
matches the system's libx264 is the whole of it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR easyworker (1)
